    "id": "mod_c12_3",
    "title": "Module 3: Secure coding",
    "description": "Secure coding is mostly about a few patterns applied every time: - validate input against what you expect; - keep data separate from code when you build queries and commands; - encode output for the context where it is displayed; - authenticate users properly; - check authorisation on every request for every object. This module teaches each pattern with standard-library Python, and proves it with security unit tests that run in the pipeline.",
